Subject: dynamic_debug-fix-documentation-errors-checkpatch-fixes
From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

ERROR: code indent should use tabs where possible
#20: FILE: include/linux/dynamic_debug.h:31:
+ ^I * writes commands to <debugfs>/dynamic_debug/control$

WARNING: please, no space before tabs
#20: FILE: include/linux/dynamic_debug.h:31:
+ ^I * writes commands to <debugfs>/dynamic_debug/control$

total: 1 errors, 1 warnings, 56 lines checked

./patches/dynamic_debug-fix-documentation-errors.patch has style problems, please review.  If any of these errors
are false positives report them to the maintainer, see
CHECKPATCH in MAINTAINERS.

Please run checkpatch prior to sending patches

Cc: Florian Ragwitz <rafl@debian.org>
Cc: Jason Baron <jbaron@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 include/linux/dynamic_debug.h |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -puN include/linux/dynamic_debug.h~dynamic_debug-fix-documentation-errors-checkpatch-fixes include/linux/dynamic_debug.h
--- a/include/linux/dynamic_debug.h~dynamic_debug-fix-documentation-errors-checkpatch-fixes
+++ a/include/linux/dynamic_debug.h
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@ struct _ddebug {
 	/*
  	 * The flags field controls the behaviour at the callsite.
  	 * The bits here are changed dynamically when the user
- 	 * writes commands to <debugfs>/dynamic_debug/control
+	 * writes commands to <debugfs>/dynamic_debug/control
 	 */
 #define _DPRINTK_FLAGS_PRINT   (1<<0)  /* printk() a message using the format */
 #define _DPRINTK_FLAGS_DEFAULT 0
_

